1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Politics is riskier for women, there is a double standard.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
We usually justify the threats to a mayor by thinking of unpopular choices or poor management,

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
but analyzing the Italian municipalities, a newly elected female mayor,

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
three times more likely to experience assaults or threats compared to a man.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
It perhaps depends on how the minister sees it, the data says otherwise.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
It means that they invest the same resources and guarantee exactly the same quality of services.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
So then, with the same results, why do they suffer this disproportionate violence?

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
It is pure discrimination. They come to pick regardless of how they work,

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
even when the minister is not clearly better than their colleagues.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The goal is not to influence local laws, but to punish the female figure in power.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
A tactic that works. For fear of retaliation, the assaulted administrators almost always give up running for office again.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
This is why women struggle to maintain leadership roles.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Today the main problem is not making things easier, but surviving a system that physically tries to push them out.
